Thread replies and reactions
Membership checks
Public and private channel access
Unread and read-state behavior
Notification persistence and deduplication
ERP entity-link authorization
Approval authorization and stale workflow state
Concurrent or repeated approval actions
Attachment access restrictions
RLS isolation between authorized and unauthorized users
Realtime reconnect and duplicate-event handling
Run the available database tests, unit tests, integration tests, type checks, lint checks, and relevant build checks.
Add or update browser-level tests for the primary employee messaging and approval flows when the project supports them.
Do not claim browser verification if the application was not actually exercised in a browser.
14. Implementation sequence
Work in this order:
Repository assessment and implementation plan.
Existing schema and workflow mapping.
Database migrations and security policies.
Messaging data-access and server-side validation.
Core chat UI and Realtime integration.
Notifications and unread/read state.
Approval inbox using existing workflow services.
ERP record links and contextual previews.
Automated tests, security review, and UI polish.
Final verification and implementation report.
Keep each phase coherent and testable. Do not rewrite unrelated ERP modules.
If a required schema, permission rule, or workflow contract is unclear, investigate the repository and document the uncertainty. Do not silently invent business rules.
15. Completion criteria
The feature is ready for review when:
Authorized ERP employees can exchange messages in real time.
Direct conversations, groups, and channels persist across refreshes.
Private content is inaccessible to unauthorized users.
Unread counts and notifications reflect persisted state.
The approval inbox uses real ERP workflow records and actions.
Approval decisions are permission-checked, auditable, and concurrency-safe.
ERP record links preserve existing access controls.
The interface follows the existing ERP design system.
Migrations, tests, type checks, lint, and build checks have been run as applicable.
Known failures and untested areas are explicitly documented.
